From 1611048a7c08b6127dd20101b51571d63aaacdeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:49:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(turn lease): a release that hit a busy state.db no longer
 blocks the next turn for 5 min [daveey]

DurableTurnLease.release only logged an ERROR when its DELETE lost the
state.db write lock, so the finished turn's row stayed until its 300 s
TTL. A same-process holder is never "dead", and Desktop/TUI admit with
wait_seconds=0, so that chat's next message was refused as "another
active writer" (self-heal agent-db9dfa2d4e, MacBook 2026-10-28 16:03 PT).

- release_session_turn_lease marks the holder abandoned (per process,
  keyed by db path + holder) when the DELETE fails with a lock error;
  try_acquire_session_turn_lease treats an abandoned holder's row as
  reclaimable. A live, never-abandoned same-process lease is still
  refused.
- DurableTurnLease.release logs WARNING "lease release deferred" and
  retries the DELETE on a daemon thread with backoff until the lease
  would expire; one ERROR "lease release retries exhausted" only if
  every attempt fails (coach detector signal).

Tests: four new cases in tests/hermes_state/test_session_turn_lease.py
(three fail on the previous main, the refused-live-lease guard passes on
both).
